  "merger_description": "Estia Investments Pty Ltd (**Estia**) proposes to acquire substantially all the business assets of six residential aged care homes from Anglicare SA Ltd (**Anglicare SA**):\n\n* Anglicare SA Grange\n* Anglicare SA Trott Park\n* Anglicare SA Elizabeth East\n* Anglicare SA Brompton\n* Anglicare SA Elizabeth \u2013 Dutton Court, and\n* Anglicare SA Westbourne Park\n\n(**Proposed Acquisition**).\n\nEstia is a registered provider of residential care services. Estia and its wholly owned subsidiaries currently operate over 90 residential aged care homes across Victoria, New South Wales, Queensland, and South Australia. Estia is currently majority owned by Bain Capital Private Equity.\u00a0On 22 July 2026, the ACCC determined under section 51ABZE(1) that the acquisition of Estia by a Stonepeak-led consortium may be put into effect, see https://www.accc.gov.au/public-registers/mergers-and-acquisitions-registers/acquisitions-register/stonepeak-led-consortium-estia-health.\n\nAnglicare SA is an independent not-for-profit organisation and a registered provider of care services. It operates six residential aged care homes in Adelaide (being the homes Estia Health proposes to acquire). Anglicare SA also provides other services to the community, including community aged care, NDIS services, foster care, mental health, financial counselling, community housing and support for vulnerable individuals. Anglicare SA intends to continue providing these other services following the Proposed Acquisition.\n\nEstia and Anglicare SA both operate residential aged care homes in certain areas within, and in the outer suburbs of, metropolitan Adelaide.",
